  "Partitions": {
    "+/2": "Two integers add exactly; numeric mixed/float operands convert integers with the already audited nearest-even conversion, then IEEE binary64 addition. Invalid types or nonfinite results raise badarith. A zero integer operand preserves the other integer term exactly; other boxed integer/float results are fresh.",
    "-/2": "Two integers subtract exactly. Mixed numeric operands use audited integer conversion and IEEE binary64 subtraction. Invalid types/nonfinite results raise badarith. Subtracting integer zero preserves the first integer term; other boxed results are fresh. Float signed-zero behavior is preserved.",
    "*/2": "Two integers multiply exactly; integer one preserves the other integer term and integer zero produces immediate zero. Mixed numeric operands use audited conversion and IEEE binary64 multiplication with nonfinite refusal. No integer identity shortcut applies to floats.",
    "//2": "Both operands must be numeric; integer operands use audited conversion and the result is always a fresh finite float. Integer zero denominator or nonfinite IEEE division result raises badarith. Float zero/negative-zero, underflow and conversion overflow follow the pinned finite-result check.",
    "div/2": "Only two integers and a nonzero divisor are valid. Exact quotient truncates toward zero; remaining combinations raise badarith. Small results use our immediate-word protocol and boxed quotient results are fresh.",
    "rem/2": "Only two integers and a nonzero divisor are valid. Exact remainder has the dividend sign and magnitude below the divisor. If dividend magnitude is smaller, return the actual dividend term; otherwise compute a fresh boxed result or immediate value. Invalid combinations raise badarith.",
    "band/2": "Integer-only infinite signed two-complement bitwise conjunction. Preserve exact value for all signs/magnitudes; boxed results are fresh, small values use immediate identity. All noninteger combinations raise badarith.",
    "bor/2": "Integer-only infinite signed two-complement disjunction, including negative operands. Native big-result allocation and managed Integer construction are fresh; small results use immediate identity. Noninteger combinations raise badarith.",
    "bxor/2": "Integer-only infinite signed two-complement exclusive-or for every sign/magnitude. Fresh boxed result or immediate value; noninteger combinations raise badarith."
  },
